## 9. Alerts view (Security → Alerts)

**Total open alerts (last 7d):** 674

### Severity distribution

| Severity | Count |
|---|---|
| High | 223 |
| Medium | 68 |
| Low | 383 |

### Top alerting host

`ztagateway` — 88.7% of all alerts.

### Why so many from the gateway

The gateway is on all three attack paths:
- Ingress traffic (Traefik logs every request)
- Auth decisions (Authelia emits every ACL denial)
- WAF blocks (Coraza emits every 403)

Consequently, most detections originate there. This is expected — but it also
means **noise from the gateway can hide signal from other zones**. Mitigate by
filtering the Alerts view by severity when triaging.

